			[ 'Is it cheaper to hire a self-employed cleaner?', 'Sometimes, because a sole trader has fewer overheads than a company. A company usually includes insurance for all staff, vetting, sickness cover and its own equipment, so compare what’s included rather than the price alone.' ],
			[ 'What happens if a self-employed cleaner is ill?', 'Usually the visit is cancelled or moved, because there’s nobody else to send. A cleaning company can normally arrange a cover cleaner.' ],
			[ 'Do I need to check a cleaning company’s insurance?', 'Yes. Most reputable companies are insured, but it’s still worth asking for the certificate and checking that it covers every cleaner they send to your home.' ],
			[ 'Is my cleaner self-employed or my employee?', 'It depends on the working arrangement, not just what you call it. A cleaner with several clients who chooses their own methods is usually self-employed, but if someone works only for you on your terms, check the official guidance on employment status.' ],
